[gd_scene format=3]

; The Coldstacks, west of the Choir (map offset (204.5, -69)): the frozen layer's hub, the cold archive's
; endless racks, stacked in stone galleries up to the roof. A pilgrim shrine on the floor. Its ways:
;   east, the Choir (back toward the Brink's fall);
;   up the galleries to a hatch in the roof, the Counterweight: an old lift that only rises, to the Undercroft;
;   the Calving, a high doorway on the west wall: up the metal buttress by grip, or by two rings;
;   down the well and east along the corridor under the floor, the Mere;
;   the Vault under the corridor, its way plugged with ice: dive through it (Drill), one way down;
;   the Chimney, a vent in the floor welling with slag: it burns without Heat plating; down it, the volcanic layer.

